//! Goofish (Xianyu) provider — a Rust port of the completed Python SDK
//! (`goofish-client` 0.12.0 / `goofish-parser` 0.9.9).
//!
//! Anonymous, read-only MTOP APIs only. Two execution paths share the
//! same request builders, registry, classification and parsers:
//!
//! - [`CoreClient`] — offline core over any [`Transport`] (used with
//!   `MockTransport` in tests; no network).
//! - [`GoofishClient`] — the live path. Public async methods build a
//!   plan, resolve the local runtime (the identity is generated by
//!   the server itself on first use and kept in its data directory;
//!   the serve signer is auto-discovered next to the
//!   executable or in the data directory and auto-started), sign
//!   synchronously, and POST via reqwest. Environment variables and
//!   a `goofish.json` config file remain available as optional
//!   overrides only. A genuinely missing runtime piece (the signer
//!   harness) is reported in the returned JSON *before* any network
//!   access.
//!
//! After a restriction response (verification / access denied / rate
//! limited) the client halts: later sends return a `send_halted` error
//! until [`GoofishClient::reset_send_halt`] (or the core equivalent) is
//! called — the port of the Python client's send-halt rule.

